# Runbook: {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Operational how-to for running this project's control harness. See
`README.md` for the file-layout/boundaries overview and
`HARNESS_GOVERNANCE.md` for the governance rules this runbook operates
under.

## First-time setup

1. Fill `spec.md` from the approved `fulcra-prototype-grill-me`
   artifacts (`intake/brief.md`, `architecture.md`, `plan.md`) in the
   deliverable repo.
2. Break `plan.md`'s milestones into `coordinator/milestones.md` entries
   (scope, requirement IDs, done criteria, per milestone).
3. Choose and configure provider adapter commands for Generator and
   Evaluator (see README.md's "Provider adapters" section) --
   genuinely separate sessions/processes, not one session switching
   personas.
4. `./bootstrap.sh <team-name>` to provision the minimal real Fulcra
   Workspace team files (root `role.md`/`progress.md`/`completed.md`/
   `log.md`) and print the fuller set of Workspace paths this project's
   documented contract targets (most of which are not yet automatically
   provisioned -- see README.md's "Scope note").
5. `./doctor.sh` to confirm the harness is in a runnable state before
   the first real milestone run.

## Running one milestone

```bash
export HARNESS_GENERATOR_CMD='...'
export HARNESS_EVALUATOR_CMD='...'
python coordinator/run_milestone.py --milestone M1 --deliverable ../<deliverable-repo>
```

This will:
1. Create or resume the `milestone/m1-<slug>` branch in the deliverable repo.
2. Run Generator against that branch with `HARNESS_ROLE=generator` and the milestone's scope/context. It may make multiple coherent commits.
3. Validate the clean final candidate commit's required `Harness-Candidate:` trailer, create its mandatory same-named annotated tag, and persist the candidate/tag/SHA record.
4. In remote mode, push the branch and tag to `origin`, then invoke `HARNESS_PR_CREATE_CMD` if configured. In local mode, no remote or PR is required.
5. Detach at the exact candidate SHA and run Evaluator independently; persist its verdict when `--team` is supplied.
6. Reject a merge-eligible PASS unless `overall: PASS` and, when declared, `test_runner: PASS` are both present. A local-mode PASS creates a non-fast-forward merge commit with message `harness/<milestone>: complete milestone` and a matching annotated `harness/<milestone>` completion tag. Remote merge adapters must do the same; fast-forward and rebase integration are forbidden.
7. On every terminal or failed run, upload current full-history control-harness and deliverable Git bundles to the Workspace. The default retention target is three File Store versions per `*-latest.bundle`, but never prune until the user explicitly approves it in `decisions.md`. After approval, set `HARNESS_BUNDLE_PRUNING_APPROVED=1` and provide a trusted `HARNESS_BUNDLE_PRUNE_CMD` that deletes only versions older than the newest three.

**Git/host boundary:** GitHub/GitLab/etc. are optional. Use `--git-mode local --integration-branch main` for a portable local-only harness, or `--git-mode remote` with optional trusted `HARNESS_PR_CREATE_CMD` / `HARNESS_PR_MERGE_CMD` adapters. Activity-aware watchdog behavior remains an integration adapter; the runner enforces a configurable hard role timeout and bounded retry policy.

## Handling a decision request

If a role emits `decision_request: true` (per
`schemas/decision-request.md`), work pauses on that thread. Bring the
question to the user, record their raw answer in `decisions.md`
(append-only), then update `spec.md` if the decision changes formalized
requirements before resuming.

## Unattended/scheduled operation

Read `coordinator/scheduled-operation.md` before creating a scheduler job.
After one explicit user scheduling decision, configure a main independent
Coordinator runner and delayed verifier; the user does not need to approve or
trigger each later milestone run. See `coordinator/unattended-recovery.md` for
what the verifier may/may not repair on its own.

## Resuming on a fresh machine

The control harness itself is portable (no execution history, no local
cache) -- clone this repo, re-run `./bootstrap.sh <team-name>` against
the same team name to reconnect to the existing Fulcra Workspace state,
then `./doctor.sh` before resuming milestone work.
